{#- One epistemic class's description (`store/epistemic_access.py`). Var:
    access (one of `epistemic_access.CLASSES`). -#}
{%- if access == "known" -%}
they know it: they were told it plainly, or it is common knowledge to them
{%- elif access == "suspected" -%}
they suspect it from hints or rumour, without knowing it
{%- elif access == "experienced" -%}
they were there and saw or heard it themselves
{%- elif access == "narrator_only" -%}
only the narrator knows it; this character has no way of knowing it
{%- endif -%}
